} else {
    for _, t := range textBlocks {
        writeChunkBuffered(w, chunk{Type: "text", Text: t}, &buffer, isCloudFront)
    }
}
```

The web-chat doesn't have this `extractDataPreview` call. It just sends text chunks. So the client receives text events with the JSON embedded, and needs to detect and render it client-side. On the client side, the web-chat serves the index file and must handle parsing data previews from incoming text events.

Checking the JSON extraction logic... I'm tracing through how the JSON extraction works with the text and code replacements, and it looks like it should correctly parse the data object from the message. But I'm realizing the production deployment might not be complete yet since the GitHub Actions merge just happened, so that could explain why the raw JSON is still showing up.

